{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwKCT5P4PkQtazhNvkkq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. I haven't opened the dashboard to check that the panels render, and the rule hasn't run yet.\n\n**Data:** the logs data view is time-based on `timestamp`. Its main fields are `response` (a string, so I used `response.keyword`), `bytes`, `extension`, `clientip`, `geo.src`/`geo.dest`, `machine.os`, `host`, `url`, `request` and `agent`.\n\n**Dashboard** \"EFF-4a2566a8 Web logs overview\" has four panels:\n- Total requests (a single count)\n- Requests over time (area chart)\n- Responses by status code (pie chart)\n- Average bytes by file extension (bar chart)\n\nIt is at http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-4a2566a8-web-logs-overview-8db6dd3204ae.\n\n**Rule** \"EFF-4a2566a8 5xx spike\" (id `86838c17-134d-4f09-b990-695603161c50`):\n- **Type:** an Elasticsearch query rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs`.\n- **Match:** documents whose `response.keyword` starts with `5`.\n- **Condition:** it fires when the count in a 5-minute window is above 10.\n- **Schedule:** it checks every minute.\n- **Actions:** I didn't attach any, so a firing only shows up in Kibana's alert list. It won't send a notification.\n\nThe rule was created disabled, so I enabled it in a separate step."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":149,"cache_read_input_tokens":20315,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":149},"output_tokens":511,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4eb1cb7-866c-5bbf-8d81-a8d5acd83be3","uuid":"6ac37403-3357-4604-855c-fdde0036caa9","timestamp":"2026-10-11T23:26:11.871Z","request_id":"re